course: dictionary
lesson: 10376
title: One word, many meanings: treat
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: The word treat can mean different things. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Treat others kindly» means behave towards them in a kind way.
explain: «I'll treat you to an ice cream» means I will buy you something special. The words ice cream are the clue. When a doctor or nurse treats you, they give care or medicine to help you get better.
explain: Treat can be a verb (a doing word) or a noun (a naming word). Check the sentence to see which one it is, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Treat can be a verb: «Treat others kindly» means behave kindly towards them.
fact: As a noun, a treat is something special that gives pleasure, such as a sweet, a trip or a surprise.
fact: To treat someone to something means to buy or give it to them as a special gift.
fact: Doctors and nurses treat illness and injuries, and this care is called treatment.
fact: Phrases to know: «my treat» means I will pay, and «trick or treat» is what children say at Halloween.
exercise: «Treat others kindly.» What does treat mean here? | To give medicine to a sick person | *To behave towards someone in a certain way | To buy someone a sweet | To make a cake
exercise: «I'll treat you to an ice cream.» What does treat mean here? | To put a coat on wood to protect it | *To buy or give someone something special | To make someone better | To feel sad
exercise: Mia says, «The nurse will treat my cut.» What does treat mean here? | To cut the paper neatly | *To give care so the cut gets better | To give a prize for being good | To wrap a present
test: «Going to the zoo was a real treat.» What is a treat here? | *Something special that gives pleasure | A kind of medicine | A rude word | A type of wood
test: «Doctors treated the swelling.» What does treated mean here? | Forgot all about it | Ate it up quickly | *Gave care to help it get better | Painted it bright colours
exam: Which sentence uses treat as a noun, meaning something special? | I will treat my friend to lunch. | The vet will treat the sick dog. | Treat others kindly. | *Our trip to the seaside was a real treat.
